  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The proposed prefix permutation already exists in the current workflow. The report should identify its incremental contribution and justify originality 5/10; potential 8/10 remains speculative without diagnostic-to-validation evidence.",
    "Substitution versus deletion does not isolate positional effects: replacement introduces new content, while deletion changes length and positions. Explicit positional controls remain missing.",
    "Reproduction requires exact frequency-bin boundaries, edit-count rounding, replacement sampling rules, timestamp eligibility, and handling of partially matched draws. Comparisons need the same eligible users and source positions to avoid selection bias.",
    "The pseudocode does not specify exception-safe restoration: a buffer-verification error must not prevent restoration of model modes, buffers, and RNG states.",
    "The report lacks a bounded experiment connecting diagnostic changes to pinned macro validation HR@10. Code difficulty 4/10 may underestimate matching, state preservation, and full-catalog recommendation integration."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Determine which controls can distinguish content changes from positional changes without introducing invalid padding behavior.",
      "query": "In SASRec with learned absolute positional embeddings and left-padded histories, how can history-ablation experiments separate item removal, sequence compaction, and positional effects? Investigate explicit position IDs, attention masks, and why interior padding or zero-item replacement may fail as deletion controls."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Make matched substitutions reproducible and reveal bias from failed matches or temporally implausible replacements.",
      "query": "What methods are used for popularity-matched item substitutions in sequential recommendation history perturbation diagnostics? Examine training-only frequency bins, sampling without replacement, timestamp-based availability proxies, common-support comparisons, and reporting unmatched interventions."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Assess whether the diagnostic merits its proposed potential rating and computational cost.",
      "query": "How have sequential recommendation studies validated whether history-perturbation sensitivity predicts ranking accuracy improvements? Seek controlled last-item and additive-history baselines, paired user comparisons, sampled versus full-catalog ranking checks, and safeguards against adaptive validation overfitting under limited experiment budgets."
    }
  ]
}
